window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/polo-6-aw1"]={"polo-6-aw1-120-km-h-overtaking-alert":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>To activate or deactivate a message reminding you that you are exceeding the 120km/h speed limit.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.  </p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Wizard</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“0”</strong> <br/>Then check to enable or uncheck to disable the box in<strong>“6”</strong>:<strong>“Speed warning at 120 kph (75 mph) active</strong>”.  </p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-acc-gas-pedal-button":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the RES button to act as a gas pedal while using ACC. Holding down the RES button allows the vehicle to reach a previously set speed faster than usual. (Boost ACC – Adaptive Cruise Control)  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket or OBDeleven.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. or OBDeleven.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and then click on “Select”. <strong><strong>13 – Regul Dist.</strong></strong> ” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>14117 <em>or</em></strong> <strong>20103</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – Select Byte <strong>02</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>07</strong> “Boost Function”.</p>\n<p>OBDeleven: Select <strong>“Boost Function”</strong><br/>Change from “desactivated” to “Activated”.</p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-only-in-auto-position":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables daytime running lights (DRL) only when the headlight control switch is in the “auto” position.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Daytime running lights—Daytime running lights only in the AUTO position</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_drl_auto_switch-c7669352.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-driving-school-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adds a driving-school mode view to Discover, displaying turn signals, speed, etc. (also ideal for accompanied driving).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule function list CAN-Driving_school</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school_over_threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/discoverautoecole-4d14ae9a.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the green hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, testmode, engineer mode) on Discover MIB2.  </p>\n<p>/!\\ Caution: Making certain changes in the hidden menu may cause MIB2 to freeze or no longer start /!\\  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“S12345</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Developer mode</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value<strong>“activated</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Restart MIB2, keep MENU button pressed until testmode menu appears</em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode-bfa51f40.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode2-1024x576-7a0c833c.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-intruder-alarm-with-horn":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate an alarm with horn in the event of intrusion into the vehicle, and to lock the door if it is opened using the interior handles.  </p>\n<p><strong>Warning! There are 8 lines of coding to do here. </strong> </p>\n<p><em><strong>For vehicles without original alarm! </strong></em><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Additional functions – Signalhorn ohne KL 15</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_disable_horn-34a976ae.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Anti-theft protection – Akustischer Alarm Signalhorn</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Anti-theft protection – Alarmsignal</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“frequency modulated</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Anti-theft protection – DWA Alarmverzoegerung</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“driver door contact thatcham</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 5:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Anti-theft protection – DWA Camper Modus</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 6:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Protection antivol – Sirenen Alarmzahl</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“10 alarms</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 7:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Protection antivol – Verzoegerung Panikalarm</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“2 sekunden verzoegerung</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 8:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Anti-theft Alarm System</strong></strong>”<strong> Anti-theft Alarm System</strong><br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-lane-assist-memory-function":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to store the Lane Assist function in memory. If you deactivate it, the Lane Assist will not automatically resume the next time you start up.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic socket or OBDeleven box.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program or the OBDeleven application.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (For Camera A5 5Q0 / 3Q0) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv.  Assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong>Personalization of lane dept. warning Cl. 15 on  </strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“last setting </strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (For Camera A5 2Q0):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv.  Assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“09</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong> 0-1</strong><strong>“03 Configuration_for_lane_departure_warning_Kl15, Last_setting</strong>”.</p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-off-road-mode-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add Offroad mode to Discover Pro or Discover Media with navigation.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-compass_0x15</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass_over-threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroad-700x500-1-830de5b6.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the reversing camera after it has been retrofitted to the Discover.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte <strong>19</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>4</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) Low installed (PR-KA1).”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/C25A41FA-66F7-4FC9-B7F4-1761395A1D01-1024x483-11bbd3cf.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>02</strong><br/>. Then, for bits <strong>4-5</strong>, select<em> “10 Camera Type: Rear View Camera (RVC) installed.”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The 2 pins of the reversing camera are used in the 12-pin quadlock (blue). Usable cable set: Part no. 000 979 009 E <br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-window-operation-with-ignition-off":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the windows to be operated (up/down) with the ignition off and the door open.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Access control 2—Disable FH follow-up for Class 15.</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>active</strong>,” then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Access control 2—Cancel FH access follow-up when door opens</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>not</strong> <strong>active</strong>,” then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitrecontactcoupevagcoding-1024x530-1c73d125.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-wiper-replacement-position-menu-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the wiper blade replacement position so that it can be selected from the Discover menu. Once enabled, the windshield wipers move to the operating position. </p>\n<p><em><strong>Tip</strong> for wiper replacement position without menu: switch off the ignition and hold the wiper lever in the lowest position until the wipers are in the blade replacement/maintenance position.</em> </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose <strong>“Windshield wiper-Menuesteuerung Frontwischer”</strong> / <strong>“Frontscheibenwischer-Menuesteuerung Frontwischer”.</strong><br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-think-blue-monitor-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the “Think Blue Monitor” mode: “ECO MODE” graph for MIB2.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_user_eco_rating</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the<strong>“active</strong>” value.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_user_eco_rating_over_threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the<strong>“active</strong>” value.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/thinkblue-1024x575-da2d1826.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-activate-deactivate-windshield-wipers-on-key-removal":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate windshield wiper stop when the key is removed (wipers stop directly in the position they were in) or to deactivate so that the wipers are in the parking position (in the windshield bay) when the key is removed.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong> “.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong> “.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Windshield wiper-Wischer stop bei KL15 aus</strong></strong>”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“active</strong>” (stop immediately on key removal) <em>or</em><strong>“inactive</strong>” (park position) and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-activation-of-progressive-interior-lighting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> turns interior lights (door knobs, dashboard, center console) on and off gradually. By default, interior lights are switched on and off immediately with the headlights. Activating this function will cause a slow fade effect each time the interior lights are switched on or off. (Interior Light Fade in/out)     <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Interior lighting-KL58 Einschalten mit Rampe</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/kl58rampe-e361a4ce.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>OBDeleven:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/KL58rampeOBDeleven-1fdea7c1.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-adjusting-the-soundaktor-volume":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust/deactivate the volume of the Soundaktor (speaker built into the windscreen bay to simulate a false engine noise). If you hear a squeaking or buzzing sound, or don’t like the noise, deactivate it completely. (Soundaktuator)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A9- Struct. Sound terminal</strong>“.</p>\n<p><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/> 5 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Volume of structure-borne noise actuator</strong>”<br/><br/> 6 – Adapt the value accordingly <br/>Default value: 100% <br/>If the value is set to 0, the sound amplifier is completely disabled.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6985-1024x629-a592b6b9.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-automatic-door-unlocking-with-dsg-on-p":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically unlocks all doors when the DSG automatic transmission is shifted to the “P” position.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1 –</strong> Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2 –</strong> Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on <strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on <strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>4 –</strong> Click <strong>“Security Access – 16,”</strong> then enter the code <strong>“31347”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select <strong>“Access control – Autounlock NAR”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>7 –</strong> On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select <strong>“active</strong>, <strong>“</strong> then confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-automatic-headlamps-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>, Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-automatically-folding-mirrors":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically folds mirrors when vehicle is locked. <br/><br/><br/><em>The vehicle must be equipped with the “Electrically folding mirrors (with comodo in door)” option. </em><br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access Control 2-Funk Spiegelanklappen</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access Control 2-Menuesteuerung Funk Spiegel anklappen</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><br/><strong>!!! For folding mirrors without having to hold down the remote control button </strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access Control 2-Funk Spiegelanklappung Modus</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“by look command via remote control key</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-brake-disc-drying":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the intensity of brake disc drying. If your car has a tendency to squeal when parked in wet weather, for example, the annoying drying of the disc brakes can be reduced or even completely deactivated, so that there are no scratches or squeaks.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“03- Electronic brakes</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“40304</strong>“.</p>\n<p><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>“.<br/><br/> 6 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“brake disc drying</strong>“<br/><br/> 7 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose the value accordingly to your choice: ” <strong>not activated, low, medium, high</strong> ” then validate.</p>","polo-6-aw1-change-discover-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to display another logo at launch, and a color to match the finish of your Discover Média or Pro.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte<strong>“18</strong>”<br/>Then modify the hexadecimal value of the box in<strong>“3)</strong>” of the long code:<br/><br/>00 – Default<br/>01 – Hybride<br/>02 – GTD<br/>03 – GTI (red color)<br/>04 – Blue Motion<br/>05 – E- (electric)<br/>06 – R-Line<br/>07 – R (blue color)<br/>08 – Alltrack<br/>09 – GTE</p>\n<p>If you have a bit 0-7 drop-down list, select your vehicle or modify the byte directly with the list. If your bits are hidden, modify in the binary value : </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/bits-logo-discover-be1ebdf0.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_discover_pro_look_carbon_byte18_MMI-Audi-A3-MQB-677483cb.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/hqdefault-856d3e0d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/maxresdefaulet-1024x576-1-9caa5322.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/maxresdefault-1024x768-1-76be041f.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-change-warning-thresholds-for-icy-conditions":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to select the outside temperature value for the risk of icy conditions for which the warning is displayed on the dashboard (Ice Warning).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Outsitde temperature p ice warning entry temperature</strong>” for the value at which the alert sounds to warn of frost. (Origin: 4°C)<br/>Then choose<strong>“Outsitde temperature p ice warning <strong><strong>exit</strong></strong> temperature</strong>” for the value at which the frost alert ends. (Origin: 6°C)  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the temperature value you want.</p>","polo-6-aw1-changing-the-virtual-cockpit-display":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to modify and customize the Active Info Display / Virtual Cockpit. Depending on the setting, the display of the counter and/or vmax is different. (For AID v2)  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (To change counter background) :</strong></p>\n<p>3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p>4 – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. In this drop-down menu, select the “<strong>Tube illustration</strong>” / <strong>“Tube representation”</strong> channel.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– In the “<strong>Value:</strong>” option, choose one of the 5 versions:  </p>\n<p>Version 0 :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tubes-illustration-AD2-V0-c3b0bf1d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 1:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tubes-illustration-AD2-V1-8c5def79.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 2:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tubes-illustration-AD2-V2-bd9ba44f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 3 (GTI):</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tubes-illustration-AD2-V3-2cd2209e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 4 (R):</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tubes-illustration-AD2-V4-f84aea0b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (To modify Vmax) :</strong> </p>\n<p>3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p>4 – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. In this drop-down menu, select the “<strong>Tachometer end value</strong>” channel.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– In the “<strong>Value:</strong>” option, choose one of the 6 versions:  </p>\n<p>Version 0 (Default) :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V0-681489bc.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 1 (280) :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V1-699bc5c3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 2 (240) :  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V2-aa2fd17c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 3 (300) :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V3-cb49d6b6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 4 (260 with additional speed marking) :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V4-96449c22.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Version 5 (280 with additional speed marking) :</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer-end-value-AD2-V5-d8e250ab.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/vw/polo-6-aw1/polo-6-aw1-logo-r-sur-virtual-cockpit/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Polo 6 (AW1) – Logo R sur Virtual Cockpit</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-comfort-flashing-light":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Turn signal control-Komfortblinken Blinkzyklen</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose between<strong>“3</strong>” and<strong>“5</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_clignotant_confo-f1a2f919.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Information: If, after coding, the number of flashes has not changed, on your MIB screen: CAR -&gt; Settings -&gt; Factory settings -&gt; Lighting (Your interior lighting configurations will also be reset).</em></p>","polo-6-aw1-coming-home-automatic":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically activates the Coming Home function (no need to make a headlight call).  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Comfort Illumination—Coming Home Status</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“automatic</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-compass-display-on-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to display a compass on the ODB (on-board computer), if you have GPS navigation (NAV), and to change its position on the speedo.</p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“10</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“6</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (if line 1 unavailable) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 –</strong> Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. In this drop-down menu, select the “<strong>Navigation /</strong><strong>Compass</strong>” channel.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> In the “<strong>Value:</strong>” option, select<strong>“Enabled</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (to change the compass position on the ODB) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 –</strong> Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. From this drop-down menu, select the “<strong>Compass</strong> <strong>indicator</strong>” channel.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> In the “<strong>Value:</strong>” option, select the desired value for the compass position on the ODB (default: lower position).</p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/compassbas-b76d2a41.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/compasshaut-cbdd1575.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate Corner Lights with fog lamps.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte12NL LB40-Lichtfunktion B 12</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Abbiegelicht links</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte13NL RB3-Lichtfunktion B 13</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Abbiegelicht rechts</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>","polo-6-aw1-correction-of-odb-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to correct the fuel consumption display on the On-Board Computer / Virtual Cockpit.  </p>\n<p><em>Note: The changes you make affect the display of instantaneous fuel consumption, average fuel consumption, and fuel quantity.</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click <strong> “17 – Instruments.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the <strong>Channel:</strong> <em>“Display correction of <em>consumption and operating range</em>“</em></p>\n<p><em>Set the consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g., l/100 km): Target: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9.8 / 9.73 ? 105.38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105.<br/>Example 2: Calculation based on distance per volume (e.g., MPG): Target: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24, and 95.83)       Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96</em>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/consomqb-7270c66a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Example 3: The fuel consumption reported by the ODB is 5.9 L/100 km; after testing, it is actually 6.3 L/100 km.<br/>Calculation of the rate to be entered: (6.3 * 100) / 5.9 = 106.78. The rate used will be 107%; the fuel consumption figure reported by the ODB will be approximately 0.1 L/100 km too low. </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correctionconsomib-4ec14680.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The usage is immediately updated on the Discover MIB:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correctionconsomib2-8b265c60.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-daytime-running-light-deactivation-drl-with-handbrake":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) using the handbrake.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Daytime running lights-Tagfahrlicht Dauerfahrlicht bei Handbremse abschalten</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Golf-7-5G---Desactiver-les-feux-de-jours-DRL-avec--6d661897.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-daytime-running-lights-drl-on-off-with-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate/deactivate daytime running lights (DRL) from Discover in the CAR Menu.  </p>\n<p>ATTENTION to your country’s regulations and technical inspection for daytime running lights!<br/>However, if you’re coding in your car to avoid using too much of your battery, this is a good solution…  </p>\n<p><br/>Procedure: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket or OBDeleven.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/>VCDS : </p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Daytime running lights—Tagfahrlicht—Activation possible via BAP or control sequence</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_feux_jour_drl-0a93900d.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>OBDeleven:</strong></p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdeleven09-d37c6d29.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdelevenadapt-0d774aea.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdelevenaussenlicht-0747a95f.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdeleventagfahrlicht-78f4d30c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdeleventagfahrlichtactive-e1f21fc0.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<hr/>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/activedrlvagcoding-c1ee180c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/activedrlvagcoding2-bf0103c8.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-deactivate-horn-without-ignition":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to turn the horn on or off when the ignition is off.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Additional Functions – Signalhorn ohne KL 15</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>not active</strong>” to disable it or <strong>“active”</strong> to enable it, then click “Submit.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_disable_horn-34a976ae.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-deactivate-mirrorlink":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable or remove MirrorLink from App-Connect on the MIB Discover. The MirrorLink service has not been natively available on Android since June 1, 2020. For a direct connection to Android Auto.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicle configuration-Mirror_link</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Disabled</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-deactivate-open-door-alarm-with-contact":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the alarm which is triggered when the door is opened and the contact is in position P.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Ignition active message</strong>” / ”  <strong>Message ignition active. trigger </strong>  “<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“tbd</strong>” /<strong>“No display</strong>” / “<strong>Aucun affichage</strong>” then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_ignition_active_-e1e03128.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-deactivate-right-hand-overtaking-prevention":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the ACC lane assist system, e.g. when on the freeway and there is a traffic jam in the left lane, the vehicle starts to slow down.  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic socket or OBDeleven box.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program or the OBDeleven application.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>13 –  <strong>Auto Dist. Reg</strong></strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“02</strong>”<br/>Then uncheck Bit<strong>“5</strong>”: “<strong><strong>overtaking_right_prevention</strong></strong>”</p>\n<p>OBDeleven: Select <strong>“overtaking_right_prevention”</strong><br/>Change from “activated” to “Deactivated”.</p>","polo-6-aw1-deactivate-switch-on-low-beam-message":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables the warning message or dialog prompting the driver to turn on the low beams when the headlight switch is in position 0.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/allumerfeuxdecroisement1-1024x609-756a4f05.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Außenlicht_uebergreifend-Fahrlichtwarnung_Hinweis_Konfig</strong>” / ” <strong>driving light_hint_config</strong> ”  <br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>kein_Hinweis</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/allumerfeuxdecroisement2-f3950d1b.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-deactivation-of-parking-aid-activation-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the beep when reverse gear is engaged or when parking assistance is activated manually.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong> “.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select ” <strong>Tonalité d’activation de l’aide au stationnement </strong>” / ” <strong>Park assist activation</strong> <strong>tone </strong>” / ” <strong>Aktivierungston für Einparkhilfe </strong>” from value list</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – Select ” <strong>Off”</strong> in the second value list  <br/></p>","polo-6-aw1-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to suppress the audible alarm and warning light in the Virtual Cockpit when driving without a seatbelt.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>0</strong>:<br/>Bit <strong>2-4</strong>: select <strong>“Seat Belt Warning inactive”</strong> from the drop-down list.</p>\n<p><strong><em>OR</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose <strong>“Deactivate</strong> <strong>Seat belt warning”</strong> / <strong>“</strong> <strong>Désactiver l’avertissement de ceinture”.</strong> <br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Oui</strong>” /<strong>“Yes”</strong> and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8U0_920_940_Module17_Adaptation_desactivate_seat_b-77d3b532.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-disable-am-frequency-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable the AM radio frequency on Discover (AM radio frequency is rarely used, unlike FM radio frequency).  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>14</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>1</strong> <strong>“AM_disable </strong> </p>\n<figure>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-disable-ops-warning-message":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables the message “Check Distance!” / “Please check surroundings” / “Look! Safe to move?” that appears on the Discover when parking in reverse.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding –</strong> 07”</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Click “ <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – Select Byte <strong>01</strong></p>\n<p>Clear bit <strong>5</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/gol7controlerladistance-1024x575-eff0c9e2.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep-horn":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set confirmation of door locking/unlocking with beep (alarm) or horn.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning!! There are 5 lines of code to write here—actually, 6. </strong> <em>(After programming, if it doesn’t work, enable the option on your screen in CAR – Open/Close Settings – check “Audible Confirmation”)</em> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals—Unlock acoustic feedback</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Yes</strong>” and then confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals—Lock Akustische Rückmeldung</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Yes</strong>” and then confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals-Akustische Rueckmeldung global</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals—Menuesteuerung Akustische Rückmeldung</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 5:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals—Duration of the acoustic feedback from the single horn</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose<strong>“normal</strong>” or<strong>“kurz</strong>” (for a short signal), then confirm.<br/><br/><strong><br/>!!! If your vehicle is not equipped with an alarm, here is the code you need to change to activate the horn </strong>  :<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 6:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Acknowledgement signals—Akustische Rückmeldung Signalhorn</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7559-1024x495-1f01c127.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-driving-mode-on-discover-mib2":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the “Driving Mode” (Drive Select) menu on the Discover MIB2. This may need to be enabled after replacing the MIB if the driving modes are no longer available.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_charisma</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the<strong>“active</strong>” value.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_charisma_over_threshold_high</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the<strong>“active</strong>” value.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-charima_0x17</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-charima_0x17_msg_bus</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Infotainment data bus</strong>” and then confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/driving-profile-selection-vw-810162e6.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/vw/polo-6-aw1/polo-6-aw1-driving-mode-mode-de-conduite-sur-odb/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Polo 6 (AW1) – Driving Mode (Mode de conduite) sur ODB</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-driving-mode-on-obd":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the selected driving mode (Eco, Normal, Sport, Individual, etc.) directly on the on-board computer (ODB) or Virtual Cockpit.<br/>Handy for instantly viewing the active profile without having to go through the multimedia menu. (Driving Mode / Drive Select)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte “<strong>8</strong>“<br/>. Then check bit “<strong>4</strong>” <em>(Display for Drive Program Functions in Instrument Cluster active)</em>.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/driving-profile-selection-cluster-f46b7c88.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/vw/polo-6-aw1/polo-6-aw1-driving-mode-mode-de-conduite-sur-discover-mib2/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Polo 6 (AW1) – Driving Mode (Mode de conduite) sur Discover MIB2</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-engine-start-button-pulse":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the heartbeat when the Start Engine Stop button is pressed for the keyless start option.  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>05 – Access/Start Authorization</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“ZAT_illumination_concept_mybeat_clamp58xt</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7456-0f43b3a6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>05 – Access/Start Authorization</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“ZAT_illumination_modus_mybeat_clamp58xt</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7457-aa96d69a.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7455-26181335.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-fan-speed-display-for-air-conditioning-in-auto-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to display fan speed when automatic air-conditioning mode is activated. (Climatronic fan speed display Auto mode)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“08 – Climatronic</strong>” /<strong>“08 – Auto HVAC</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“11</strong>”<br/>Then select Bit<strong>“0-1</strong>”:<strong>“Blower display in Auto mode, enabled</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/bitaffichageclimauto-48c9b868.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/affichageclimautomqba1-scaled-434fefd1.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-fender-dynaudio-logo-at-discover-start-up":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To display the Fender or Dynaudio logo when your Discover Media or Pro is launched. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Information Electr.</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then type the code<strong>“20103</strong>”<br/><br/> 5 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. <br/>From this drop-down menu, select the <strong>“Startup_Screen_Sticker_HMI”</strong> channel <strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose<strong>“1</strong>” for <em>Fender</em> or<strong>“2”</strong> for <em>Dynaudio</em>, then validate. <em>(00 01 or 00 02, 00 00 without logo)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_8989-1024x452-1b626ef0.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mib-fender-dynaudio-1024x576-5dff9a92.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-fog-light-on-open-door-side":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to ensure that when a door is opened on the left, the fog lamp on the left lights up and vice versa.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here.</strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte12NL LB40-Lichtfunktion F 12</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Tuerausstiegslicht links</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte13NL RB3-Lichtfunktion F 13</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Tuerausstiegslicht rechts</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte12NL LB40-Dimmwert EF 12</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose between<strong>“0</strong>” and<strong>“100</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte13NL RB3-Dimmwert EF 13”</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose between<strong>“0</strong>” and<strong>“100</strong>”, then confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-fully-opening-sunroof-with-the-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows the sunroof to open fully when opening with the remote control.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access control 2-SAD Richtung Komfortoeffnen</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Open”</strong> and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_sliding_roof-a62f2b37.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code <strong>“31347”</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Zugangskontrolle 2-SAD Komfort schliessen</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Active</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code <strong>“31347”</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Zugangskontrolle 2-SAD Komfort oeffnen</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Active</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4 (Optional, to open the sunroof completely):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>CA – Sunroof</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Target position for comfort opening</strong>” / “<strong>Komfortfunktionen-Ziellage bei Komfortöffnen</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but further down<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Sliding position </strong>” then click Submit.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_8953-1024x754-fa7d5332.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-headlamp-call-with-fog-lamps":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows fog lamps to be used in addition to high beam. <br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte12NL LB40-Lichtfunktion C 12</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Lichthupe generell</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte12NL LB40-Dimmwert<strong>CD12</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“100</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte13NL RB3-Lichtfunktion C 13</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Lichthupe generell</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong><strong>“Leuchte13NL RB3-Dimmwert</strong><strong>CD13</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“100</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><em>INFO: Impossible coding with a Polo 6 without AB!</em></p>","polo-6-aw1-hill-start-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set Hill Start Assist operation. (hill-start assist)   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong><strong>Brakes </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Hill Start assistant</strong>” / “Assistant démarrage en côte”.<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong> On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the value based on your preference:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>“<strong>normal</strong>” (default value)</li>\n<li>“<strong>Early</strong>” (faster triggering)</li>\n<li>“<strong>Late”</strong> triggering</li>\n</ul>\n<p>then click “Submit.”</p>","polo-6-aw1-increase-gas-pedal-sensitivity":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to increase accelerator pedal sensitivity. (better acceleration response with DSG, more significant than with manual).  <br/><br/>Proceed : <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“44 – Steering Assistance</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“19249</strong>“.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Commutation profil de conduite</strong>” /<strong>“Driving profile switchover</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose the value: “<strong><em>directly: controlled by threshold value</em></strong>” / “<em><strong>Direct controlled over threshold value</strong></em>” then confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7198-330b03e4.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-increase-the-distance-between-curb-and-car-park-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to set the distance between the curb and the car during Park Assist.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“10 – Park/Steer Assist</strong>” / <strong>“10 – Assistance stationnt”.</strong><br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose <strong>“Abstand zum Bordstein” / “Distance to curb</strong>” / <strong>“Ecart avec la bordure”.</strong><br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select the distance of your choice (in cm). The default value is “<strong>15 cm</strong>“; then click “Confirm.” </p>","polo-6-aw1-interior-lighting-deactivated-when-trunk-is-opened":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> deactivates interior lighting when only the trunk is opened.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Interior lighting Innenlicht-bei offenem Heckdeckel einschalten</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“inactive</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-key-operation-even-with-ignition-on":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to use the key and lock the vehicle with the ignition switched on or the engine running. (Very practical with a Keyless Kessy key)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access control-Funk bei Klemme 15 ein</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","polo-6-aw1-lap-timer":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add the stopwatch to the ODB/Virtual Cockpit.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Lap Timer active</strong>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GOLF-7-VAGCOM---CHECK-DES-AIGUILLES-1-dab4b41b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Alternative method if the 1st doesn’t work!! :</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Lap counter</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Display</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_lap_timer-1024x576-47b6d57a.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-light-assist-always-active":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically activates the high beam assistant on start-up if it was active before the ignition was switched off.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Assistance light functions-Fernlichtassistent Reset</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“not active</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/fernlicht-6b04f01d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/lightassist-1a9a5499.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To lock/unlock the Discover CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against CD theft.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“5F – Information Electr.</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong><strong><em>“Ejector lock</em></strong> / <strong><em>“Auswurfssperre</em></strong><em> </em></strong></em>/ <strong><em>“CD Eject Button </em></strong>then set the value to <strong><strong>Active</strong></strong> <em>for eject lock.</em></p>\n<p>To eject the CD/DVD, set the value to <strong>Off</strong> for normal use of the button.</p>","polo-6-aw1-microphone-sensitivity-adjustment":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the intensity of the hands-free system’s microphone.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Microphone sensitivity</strong>” or “<strong>Mikrofonempfindlichtkeit</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value expressed in<strong>“dB</strong>” (default value<strong>“0 dB</strong>”) then validate.<br/></p>","polo-6-aw1-mirror-folding-adjustment-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to set the option to fold the side mirrors using the remote control when locking the vehicle. <br/><br/><br/><em>The vehicle must be equipped with the “Power-folding side mirrors” option</em> <em>!</em> <br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<em><br/></em><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Access Control 2-Funk Spiegelanklappung Modus</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the value that suits your needs, then confirm.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Default: <strong>“by convenience operation via remote control key”</strong> = press and hold the button on the key fob to fold the outside mirrors.</li>\n<li>Alternative: <strong>“by look command via remote control key”</strong> “by looking command via the remote control key” = briefly press the button on the key fob to fold the side mirrors.</li>\n</ul>","polo-6-aw1-modify-power-steering-hardness":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the hardness of the power steering for a softer steering wheel (Comfort) or a harder sporty one (Dynamic). <br/>Warning: if you have the driving mode selection, do not modify! <br/><br/><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. Procedure: 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“44 – Steering Assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“19249</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/> 6 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Courbes caractéristiques d’assistance de direction</strong>” /<strong>“Characteristic curve of steering assistance</strong>”<br/><br/> 7 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose the value:<strong>“Confort</strong>” or <strong>“Dynamic”</strong> then validate.</p>\n<p>selection_by_charisma: You have the driving modes, do not modify this value otherwise you will lose the hardness of the steering wheel according to your driving mode!  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/steeringassistance-1024x506-c5ba8daa.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/assistancedirection-scaled-eed591de.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the scanning of the speedometer needles when the car is started. (Works with Virtual Cockpit) (Needle Sweep)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“0</strong>”:<strong>“Gauge Test/Needle Sweep (Stading) active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GOLF-7-VAGCOM---CHECK-DES-AIGUILLES-1-dab4b41b.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-oil-temperature-on-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to display oil temperature on the ODB/Virtual Cockpit.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“10</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“1</strong>”:<strong>“Display Oil Temperature</strong>”.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/temperature-huile-vagcoding-ef203ab4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/temphuileg7-1024x768-7b5d2875.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-r-logo-on-virtual-cockpit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to display an R logo on the Active Info Display / Virtual Cockpit. (For AID v2)  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu. From this drop-down menu, select the “<strong>R Logo</strong>” channel.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– In the “<strong>Value:</strong>” option, choose one of the 4 versions  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>R logo</li>\n<li>R-Line logo</li>\n<li>R logo (New)</li>\n<li>R-Line logo (New)</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/R-LOGO-ec4ff921.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/vw/polo-6-aw1/polo-6-aw1-modifier-laffichage-du-virtual-cockpit/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Polo 6 (AW1) – Modifier l’affichage du Virtual Cockpit</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","polo-6-aw1-rear-lights-activated-with-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rear lights to turn on when the daytime running lights (Scandinavian DRL) are activated (This method turns on the instrument panel lights) <br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Daytime running lights—Tagfahrlicht—Dauerfahrlicht activated in addition to parking lights</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu near the bottom of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>active</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_feux_arriere_drl-eff83f7a.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-make-up-quantity-display-on-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the amount of fuel needed to completely fill your tank on the ODB / Virtual Cockpit. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“, then on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>10</strong>“<br/>. Then check bit “<strong>4</strong>“: “Volume to Be Replenished”</p>\n<p>If it’s a hidden bit, you need to replace the <strong>0</strong> with a <strong>1</strong> in “<strong>Binary</strong>.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Golf-MKVII-Affichage-quantite-carburant-ODB-1024x3-6098b6ed.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/refuel-quantity-golf7-504de88f.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-reprogramming-a-new-battery":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to reprogram or recode all data for the new battery after it has been replaced. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Nominal Battery Capacity</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the rated capacity listed on your battery. For example: “<strong>70Ah</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Battery Technology</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu further down<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the corresponding value<br/>. For example: For the VARTA E39, select “<strong>Etoffe</strong>” / “<strong>Fleece</strong>” for AGM.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Battery Manufacturer</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu further down the page<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the corresponding brand:<br/>For example: For the VARTA E39, select “<strong>VAO</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Configuration—Battery Serial Number</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>In this menu, enter the corresponding serial number:<br/>Note: Enter only the <strong>last 10 digits</strong> of the serial number.<br/></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Battery Status Detection Features:</strong></p>\n<p><br/>Battery status detection in the battery data module calculates the following quantities, which are transmitted via the LIN bus to the J533 data bus diagnostics interface:<br/>1 “Battery non-existent” detection: if the battery data module detects no battery for<br/>more than 30s, a corresponding bit is set to a<br/>2 voltage momentarily allowing optimum charging of the battery<br/>3 “Motor startability” bit. This indicates whether or not the battery is momentarily able to start<br/>the engine<br/>4 charge that can momentarily still be drawn from the battery before reaching the<br/>engine startability limit<br/>5 current state of charge of the battery<br/>6 battery ageing. Battery ageing can be determined via quantities such as energy storage capacity and momentary battery power.<br/>7 battery quiescent voltage<br/>8 battery internal resistance  </p>\n<p><strong>The battery sensor in the J367 battery monitoring control unit:</strong></p>\n<p>Knowing whether the battery has enough electrical energy to restart the engine is essential for the start-stop system to function properly.<br/>The control module is located directly on the “negative” terminal of the ground wire and is connected to the diagnostic interface via the LIN data bus.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/charge-batterie-c76863ff.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Signal Usage:</strong><br/>The battery sensor records the following values:<br/>– Battery temperature<br/>– Battery voltage<br/>– Charging current<br/>The battery temperature is calculated using a lookup table and the ambient temperature.<br/>It also allows for estimates of the battery’s charging time.<br/>Using the data obtained in this way, it is possible to adjust the charging control—particularly the charging voltage—to the battery’s state of charge and operating conditions. The goal is to increase the availability of the start-stop system by optimally utilizing data from the starter battery. </p>\n<p><strong>Consequences in the Event of a Malfunction</strong><br/>If the battery sensor is defective, the battery status can no longer be detected correctly.<br/>A fault is logged in the diagnostic interface’s fault memory. The start-stop system is deactivated. </p>\n<p><strong>Battery</strong></p>\n<p>The vehicle’s battery is housed in the engine compartment and protected by a battery tray. The size and type of battery depend on the engine version, equipment, and country-specific variant. Standard batteries, EFB batteries, and AGM batteries are used.<br/>Vehicles with gasoline engines and start/stop systems are equipped with an EFB battery, while vehicles with diesel engines and start/stop systems are equipped with an AGM battery. Vehicles with auxiliary heaters typically have an AGM battery.   </p>\n<p><strong>EFB</strong></p>\n<p>An EFB battery (short for Enhanced Flooded Battery) is a reinforced flooded battery. The positive plate inside the battery is coated with an additional layer of polyester mesh. This provides the battery’s active material with additional support on the plate. These batteries have greater resistance to charge-discharge cycles than standard batteries. During charging, an EFB battery is treated like a standard battery.    </p>\n<p><strong>AGM Battery</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-agm-f4b81a74.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In AGM (Absorbent Glass Mat) batteries, the battery electrolyte is retained within a microporous glass mat. An AGM battery is characterized not only by even greater resistance to charge-discharge cycles compared to an EFB battery, but also by its leak-proof design. When charging, follow the charger’s user manual and, if applicable, select the AGM battery program.  </p>\n<p>In the case of AGM batteries, the automotive battery electrolyte is retained in a micro-porous glass mat. In addition to<br/>increased resistance to alternating cycles, an AGM battery is characterized by its good sealing properties. Waterproofing is of crucial importance<br/>, especially when the battery is installed in the passenger compartment. When charging, please follow the charger’s operating instructions and select the program for<br/>AGM battery, if applicable.   </p>\n<p>Below, we can see the brand, serial number, and manufacturer of the battery</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-124711ff.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-set-acc-control-in-1-km-h-increments":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to adjust the ACC distance setting from the factory setting so that it can be set in 1 km/h increments by pressing the switch.  </p>\n<p>By default, the PLUS and MINUS buttons on the adaptive cruise control system adjust your speed in 10 km/h increments. You can change the coding in 1 km/h increments by briefly pressing the button. And use the old 10 km/h speed increments by pressing and holding the buttons.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and then click on “Select”. <strong><strong>13 – Regul Dist.</strong></strong> ” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>14117 <em>or</em></strong> <strong>20103</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – Select Byte <strong>02</strong></p>\n<p>Select bit <strong>6</strong> “Operation Mode 2”.</p>\n<p>Some speed controller modules may use a different coding or even have this parameter as an adaptation instead of the coding. Make sure that the option you are about to modify is correctly labeled.</p>\n<p>Module 13 → Adaptation → Mode de fonctionnement / Operation Mode → Mode de fonctionnement 2 / Operation Mode 2</p>","polo-6-aw1-speed-of-radar-deactivation-or-reversing-camera":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Selects the speed at which the radar and/or reversing camera are deactivated.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Switch-off speed for parking assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value between<strong>“0</strong>” and<strong>“15</strong>” km/h, depending on your preference.</p>","polo-6-aw1-start-stop-deactivation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable Start and Stop completely.  <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Watch out! There are 1 or 2 lines of coding to do here, depending on the method.</strong> <em>(After 2019 deactivation no longer works according to gateway reference “AA”)  </em></p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket or OBDeleven.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Procedure: 1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket:</p>\n<p><strong>VCDS :  </strong><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose <strong>“Limite de tension de départ marche/arrêt” / “Start/Stop voltage limit”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“12</strong>” (default value = <strong>7.6V</strong>) then validate.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_start_stop_change_voltage_limit_value-a50bc29b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><strong>OBDeleven:</strong></strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdelevenstartstoptension-ec0170bc.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>YouTube video:</strong></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Method 2 (Temperature method):</strong></p>\n<p><strong>VCDS :</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Start/Stopp Auntemperaturvorgabe-Minimaltemperatur</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“50</strong>” (default value = <strong>-50.0</strong>) and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Start/Stopp Auntemperaturvorgabe-Maximaltemperatur</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“50</strong>” (default value = <strong>-50.0</strong>) and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong><strong>OBDeleven:</strong></strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/obdelevenstarstoptemp-494422ad.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-third-brake-light-on-when-trunk-is-open":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to keep the 3rd brake light on if the trunk is not fully closed. For security lighting at night or to make sure your safe is securely closed.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte22BR MC9-Lichtfunktion C 22</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, select the value<strong>“Heckdeckel Offen</strong>” and confirm. <em>(Origin: nicht aktiv)</em><br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Leuchte22BR MC9-Dimmwert CD 22</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value between<strong>“0</strong>” and<strong>“100</strong>” depending on the power of the brake light, then confirm. <em>(Origin: 0)</em></p>","polo-6-aw1-activate-fog-lamps-as-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the daytime running lights (DRL) to turn on along with the fog lights.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Leuchte12NL LB40-Lichtfunktion B 12</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Daytime running lights</strong>” and then confirm.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_drl_with_fog_lig-cbaa08b2.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Leuchte13NL RB3-Lichtfunktion B 13</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Daytime running lights</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5Q0-937-084-Q_Module09_Adaptation_drl_with_fog_lig-f4968343.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-vehicle-modification-in-the-virtual-cockpit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to modify the vehicle on the Active Info Display / Virtual Cockpit.  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“02</strong>“<br/>Then select Bit<strong>“3-6</strong>“: ” “.<strong><strong>Model: Variant X</strong></strong>“<br/><br/>Choose the <strong>Variant</strong> corresponding to the desired vehicle.</p>\n<p>Example of a Variant :</p>\n<p>Variant 2: Golf 7 GTI 5-door<br/>Variant 3: Golf 7 GTI 3-door <br/>Variant 6: Golf 7R 5-door<br/>Variant 7: Golf 7R 3-door<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/modelvariant-45e3c204.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Variant-362e1ca0.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/variantgolf7-b2caa38a.webp\"/></figure>","polo-6-aw1-windows-close-automatically-when-locked":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically closes the windows when the car is locked. A new menu will be activated in door settings to deactivate the option if required.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “ZV Komfort Fensterheber – Komfortschliessen Brasilien”.<strong><strong>ZV Komfort Fensterheber – Komfortschliessen Brasilien</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“31347</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“ZV Komfort Fensterheber – <strong>BAP Komfortschliessen Brasilien</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>"};
